WEBVTT

00:03:29.417 --> 00:03:31.976
from my brother's and sister's room,
tangled in wires,

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.809
and now I had something to show them.

00:03:33.833 --> 00:03:36.143
So I brought them
into the living room one night,

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:38.309
it was probably 1991,
somewhere around there,

00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:40.351
and I sit them down in the living room --

00:03:40.375 --> 00:03:42.726
my heart was pounding,
my breaths were deep --

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.268
sort of like right now --

00:03:44.292 --> 00:03:45.768
and I pressed play

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:49.684
and something extraordinary
happened actually.

00:03:49.708 --> 00:03:50.958
They cried.

00:03:51.583 --> 00:03:52.851
And cried.

00:03:52.875 --> 00:03:56.226
They cried not because it was
the most amazing home video edit ever --

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.768
although it was pretty good --

00:03:57.792 --> 00:03:58.768
(Laughter)

00:03:58.792 --> 00:04:04.226
but because they saw our family
as a normal family that fit in